{
  "compilerOptions": {
    "target": "ES2020",
    "useDefineForClassFields": true,
    "lib": ["ES2020", "DOM", "DOM.Iterable"],
    "module": "ESNext",
    "skipLibCheck": true,
    "moduleResolution": "bundler",
    "allowImportingTsExtensions": true,
    "resolveJsonModule": true,
    "isolatedModules": true,
    "noEmit": true,
    "jsx": "react-jsx",
    "strict": true,
    // ── `noUnusedLocals` — ON. IT CATCHES A DECLARATION NOTHING READS. ─────────
    //
    // ⚠️ **THE SENTENCE THAT STOOD HERE CARRIED A WRONG BREAKDOWN, AND IT IS
    // CORRECTED RATHER THAN REPEATED.** It read *"28 sites, 27 of them dead
    // imports … and one real dead const"*. The 28 was right; the split was not.
    // Derived at adoption, on the surface `tsconfig.json` covers:
    //   · 19 unused IMPORT specifiers (`React` ×3, lucide icons, `useEffect` /
    //     `useState` / `useMemo`, four type-only imports)
    //   ·  4 local TYPE ALIASES  (`BuyerDiscovery`: Region/Category/SortKey/ToggleId)
    //   ·  3 module-scope CONSTS (`SERIES_BY_ROOT`, `TOKEN_WARNING`, `TOKEN_DANGER`)
    //   ·  1 destructured BINDING (`CommHubInbound` · `supplierName`)
    //   ·  1 FUNCTION declaration (`supplierApplicationStore` · `clone`)
    // The SPEC surface adds 11 more (`tsconfig.vitest.json` inherits this flag —
    // it is set ONCE, here, and a second copy there would be a figure that can
    // drift). 39 in total, and a fixpoint: removing them cascaded once, onto
    // `fixturePresent.guard.test.ts` · `docStateAt`, whose only reader was one of
    // the 39.
    //
    // ⚠️ **NOT ONE OF THE 39 WAS A LIVE DEFECT, AND THAT WAS CHECKED RATHER THAN
    // ASSUMED** — a dead declaration can be the visible end of a half-removed
    // feature, so each was resolved against something other than its own file.
    // The three that came closest, and what settled them:
    //   · `clone` (the application store) — read as "this store leaks internal
    //     rows by reference". Derived against ALL TWELVE sibling stores: `clone`
    //     is used at exactly two sites in each, seeding `rows` from a fixture and
    //     re-seeding in `reset()`, and at NO read path anywhere. This store seeds
    //     `[]` by ruling, so both call sites never existed. Nothing diverges.
    //   · `sourceableRequisitions` (BuyerSourcing) — a FILTER imported and never
    //     called reads as a page showing rows it should have narrowed. The
    //     narrowing moved to the seam, and the seam demonstrably applies it:
    //     `MockProcurementService.getRequisitions` filters on `filter.status`,
    //     which the page supplies from the machine's own from-states.
    //   · `docsCoherentAt` (fixturePresent.guard) — defined, never asserted, while
    //     its twin `oblsCoherentAt` carries five assertions. Its retirement is
    //     QUOTED into that file with the reason, the measurement (82 anchors
    //     satisfied it) and the trade. The helper outlived the quotation.
    // Two more left a comment that deletion would have stranded, so the comment
    // went with the code: `meaningWideOf`'s doc promised results *"MEASURED and
    // reported below"* that nothing computed, and the R-B gate said a declined
    // field is *"DECLINED AND REPORTED"* when only the decline was real.
    //
    // ⚠️ **THE SPECIMEN CHECK CAME BACK NEGATIVE — THE SECOND CONSECUTIVE ONE,
    // AND THE TWO FAIL FOR THE SAME REASON.** This flag was dispatched as the
    // guard for #333's class: bindings that survived a locale/anchor branch and
    // had to be deleted by hand. Measured at THREE commits — `77bd9ab` (#333's
    // parent), `270a06b` (#333) and `63a49cc` (#334) — the flag reports **28
    // errors at each, the same 28 members as today, and names NOTHING in any of
    // the nine surfaces #333 touched.** The reason is structural: the bindings
    // #333 deleted were READ — `nowIso` had four readers in `SupplierDashboard`
    // and seven in `BuyerContracts` — they were live and WRONG, not dead.
    // Together with #346's negative result on #341, the shape is now stated
    // rather than rediscovered: **TS6133/TS6196 answer "is this declaration
    // reached?", never "is what it computes correct?"** A wrong value with a
    // reader is outside this family's reach in both directions.
    //
    // ⚠️ **AND THERE IS NO ESCAPE HATCH. MEASURED, BECAUSE `noUnusedParameters`
    // HAS ONE AND THE SYMMETRY IS FALSE.** A probe declaring `_underscoreLocal`,
    // `_innerUnderscore` and `type _UnusedTypeAlias` under this flag reports an
    // error on ALL THREE: an underscore prefix silences an unused PARAMETER and
    // does nothing for a local. The one real exemption is narrower and is not
    // about the name — an unused binding in an OBJECT DESTRUCTURE THAT HAS A REST
    // ELEMENT is allowed (the omit-a-property idiom), which is why the probe's
    // `const { a, ...rest }` passed while `const { supplierId, supplierName }`
    // above did not. **So a deliberately dead local cannot be kept with a stated
    // reason the way `docCount(_c: Contract)` is kept above.** If one is ever
    // genuinely wanted, it costs a real reference or an amendment here — not a
    // rename. That is a stricter flag than its sibling, and the strictness is
    // recorded so the next seat does not reach for a hatch that is not there.
    "noUnusedLocals": true,
    // ── `noUnusedParameters` — ON, and here is what it is for. ───────────────
    //
    // It catches A PARAMETER WHOSE SIGNATURE ASSERTS A USE THE BODY DOES NOT
    // MAKE. On adoption it found exactly one site tree-wide, and the site was a
    // real defect: `data/communicationProfiles.ts`'s GERMAN `asn_reminder` took
    // `supplier` and never interpolated it, addressing an unnamed recipient
    // while holding the name. Nine sibling locales used it, and so did the
    // German `po_issued` template TWENTY LINES ABOVE IT — so the fix was the
    // file's own convention (`Sehr geehrte Damen und Herren von ${supplier}`),
    // not a translation decision.
    //
    // ⚠️ **THE SPECIMEN CHECK, AND IT CAME BACK NEGATIVE — RECORDED RATHER THAN
    // OMITTED.** This flag was dispatched as the guard that would have caught
    // #341. It would NOT have. Measured, not reasoned: a worktree at `3b062aa`
    // (#341's parent, where `obligationCount: number` / `obligationsMet: number`
    // still stood unread) reports ONE error under this flag — the same German
    // template — and says nothing about either field. **TS6133 cannot reach an
    // interface member**, so a stored field with no reader is outside this
    // flag's reach by construction, in both directions.
    //
    // The instrument for THAT class already exists and is already gated: C11
    // **V11** / `src/lib/storedFieldGate/`. ⚠️ It did not catch #341 either, and
    // the reason is worth knowing before anyone leans on it: its population is
    // derived from `GLOSSARY_REGISTRIES`' source types — 25 CLOSED STRING-LITERAL
    // UNIONS, not entity DTOs — so a field typed `number` on a DTO exposing none
    // of them was never in its population. Filed; not this batch.
    //
    // THE ESCAPE HATCH IS `_`-PREFIX. Seven parameters use it today and ALL SEVEN
    // WERE AUDITED ON ADOPTION — because a parameter renamed to `_x` to silence a
    // check is this defect wearing the fix's clothes, and an unaudited hatch is
    // where it would live. They fall in two kinds, neither of them that:
    //   · FIVE are INTERFACE OBLIGATIONS — the signature is someone else's.
    //     `_toState` ×3 (`CommandTarget.create` / `.applyTransition`), `_svc` ×2
    //     (the scoped-hook callback shape).
    //   · TWO are DELIBERATE SINGLE-SEAT SEAMS whose reason is stated AT THE SITE,
    //     which is what separates them from the German template above — that one
    //     stated nothing and contradicted its own file. `docCount(_c: Contract)`
    //     returns 0 "by construction: the portal links no documents to a contract
    //     today", kept as a function so a real relation has one seat to land in;
    //     `FOOTER_VARIANT(_r: RFQ)` returns `'outline'` because §68 retired the
    //     solid register, and it is PINNED — `BuyerSourcing.footer.test.ts` holds
    //     nine assertions against it, so the seam cannot quietly rot.
    // The discriminator, for the next one: a hatch is honest when the signature is
    // owed to a caller or the emptiness is stated and pinned. Silence is not.
    "noUnusedParameters": true,
    "noFallthroughCasesInSwitch": true,
    "allowSyntheticDefaultImports": true,
    "esModuleInterop": true
  },
  "include": ["src"],
  "exclude": ["src/**/*.test.ts", "src/**/*.test.tsx", "src/test"]
}
